What are the keys to success in NetHack?

For me, frustration and fascination lie very close together in this 
game; the latter being the reason that I usually return to a period of 
playing NetHack two or three times a year, but yet again abandon it 
due to lack of success, and consequently forget a portion of acquired 
knowlegde over time as a result.
The learning curve is extremly shallow in my opinion. I never got far 
in the game. Quite soon the monsters just get too tough/dangerous for 
me. That zoo at Sokoban's end! Those Yetis in the Rogue Level! Gees! 
Yikes!

It's seems, that most folks ascend but me. Are you all Wunderkinder?

